    "alert_id": "DTG_WEIGHT_GAIN_001",
    "title": "Significant weight gain on DTG with metabolic consequences",
    "message": "Guidelines list rapid weight gain as a risk factor for developing diabetes in PLHIV and recommend weight management for at-risk patients. This patient gained 17 kg (65 to 82 kg) with BMI rising from 25.6 to 32.4 kg/m² within 18 months of switching to DTG. Waist circumference is 96 cm. DTG is associated with significant weight gain. The weight gain has coincided with new-onset pre-diabetes, dyslipidemia, and elevated blood pressure, compounding cardiovascular risk. Guidelines recommend prescribing metabolically neutral ARVs (ABC, TDF, 3TC) for patients at risk of developing DM.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Consider switching DTG to a metabolically neutral regimen. Initiate structured weight loss counseling including diet, exercise, and smoking cessation if applicable.",
