    "alert_id": "MONITORING_GAP_001",
    "title": "Missing clinician assessment and plan for abnormal labs",
    "message": "Guidelines require clinician assessment when adverse events are suspected on DTG, including checking glucose and clinical management based on symptoms and signs. The DTG monitoring flowchart triggers assessment for weight changes and symptoms interfering with daily activities. This patient reports weight gain and fatigue with abnormal glucose, HbA1c, and lipids, yet no assessment or plan was documented. Required actions include diabetes screening, lipid management evaluation, and blood pressure follow-up. The treatment goal for blood pressure is <140/90 mmHg; this patient is at 138/88 mmHg, borderline.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Document clinical assessment addressing weight gain, fatigue, pre-diabetes, dyslipidemia, and borderline BP. Order follow-up fasting glucose and lipid panel. Provide lifestyle counseling.",
