    "alert_id": "DYSLIPIDEMIA_001",
    "title": "New-onset dyslipidemia with atherogenic profile",
    "message": "Guidelines identify dyslipidemia as a risk factor for diabetes in PLHIV and recommend weight management and lifestyle modification. This patient has total cholesterol 228 mg/dL, LDL 148 mg/dL, HDL 38 mg/dL, and triglycerides 212 mg/dL, all abnormal. No baseline lipids are available for comparison, but the current profile is atherogenic. DTG and TDF can contribute to lipid changes, though dietary and genetic factors may also play a role. Combined with obesity, pre-diabetes, and family history of diabetes, this significantly increases cardiovascular risk. No lipid management plan was documented.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
